@page "/docs/get-started/ai-assistants"

@* Connecting an AI assistant to IzzyBlazor's docs: the MCP server at /mcp (Services/Mcp), llms.txt
   and the API metadata. The client settings were the documented ones for each client in Oct 2026. *@

<ArticlePage Section="get-started" Slug="ai-assistants">
    <Lead>
        An AI assistant guesses at a library it hasn't seen, and IzzyBlazor is newer than its training data. When you
        connect your assistant to IzzyBlazor's MCP server, it looks up components, parameters and working examples for the
        release this site documents instead.
    </Lead>
    <ChildContent>
        <Heading Level="2">The server</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            The server's URL is <Code>@Endpoint</Code>. It uses the Streamable HTTP transport and doesn't need a sign-in or
            key. Its tools only read the docs. Its answers cover the release this site documents.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">Claude Code</Heading>
        <Code Block Language="bash">claude mcp add --transport http izzyblazor @Endpoint</Code>
        <TextBlock>
            To share the server with everyone on the project, add <Code>--scope project</Code>. Claude Code then saves it in
            the repository's <Code>.mcp.json</Code>.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">VS Code and Visual Studio</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            In VS Code, add the server to <Code>.vscode/mcp.json</Code>. In Visual Studio, add it to <Code>.mcp.json</Code>
            next to the solution. Then use it from Copilot's agent mode:
        </TextBlock>
        <Code Block Language="json" Title=".vscode/mcp.json">@VsCodeJson</Code>

        <Heading Level="2">Cursor</Heading>
        <Code Block Language="json" Title=".cursor/mcp.json">@CursorJson</Code>

        <Heading Level="2">Claude apps</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            In Claude's desktop app or on claude.ai, open Settings, then Connectors, add a custom connector and paste
            <Code>@Endpoint</Code>. Any other client that supports Streamable HTTP uses the same URL.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">Tools</Heading>
        <Table Items="Tools" Caption="Tools" Size="ControlSize.Sm" Class="site-params" Bordered="false">
            <Columns>
                <TemplateColumn Title="Tool" Width="Length.Rem(10)"><code>@context!.Name</code></TemplateColumn>
                <TemplateColumn Title="Answers with">@context!.Answers</TemplateColumn>
    
            </Columns>
        </Table>
        <TextBlock>
            The tools answer in Markdown, with links to this site. Describe what you're building, such as "a settings form
            that posts on static pages", and the assistant picks the tools. To help it use them, name IzzyBlazor in your
            request.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">Without MCP</Heading>
        <List Gap="2">
            <ListItem>
                <Anchor Href="llms.txt">llms.txt</Anchor>: describes IzzyBlazor and links to every article and component, for
                assistants that read websites.
            </ListItem>
            <ListItem>
                <Anchor Href="izzyblazor.api.json">API metadata</Anchor>: every component's parameters, events, methods and
                types in one JSON file, for your own tools.
            </ListItem>
        </List>

        <Heading Level="2">Next steps</Heading>
        <List Gap="2">
            <ListItem><Anchor Href="docs/get-started/create-app">Create an app</Anchor>: <Code>--mcp</Code> connects the new app to the server.</ListItem>
            <ListItem><Anchor Href="docs/common/render-modes">Render modes</Anchor>: what components do on static and interactive pages.</ListItem>
        </List>
    </ChildContent>
</ArticlePage>

@code {
    private const string Endpoint = "https://izzyblazor.com/mcp";

    private sealed record Tool(string Name, string Answers);

    private static readonly Tool[] Tools =
    [
        new("search", "Components, parameters, types, examples and articles that match the search words"),
        new("list_components", "Every component by category, with a summary and any render mode limits"),
        new("get_component", "A component's API: parameters with types and defaults, events, methods, render mode support, parts, example ids and accessibility"),
        new("get_type", "An enum's values, a type's members, or the shared style props"),
        new("get_example", "An example's whole .razor source"),
        new("get_article", "An article or a component's Overview, with its examples' source"),
    ];

    private const string VsCodeJson = """
        {
          "servers": {
            "izzyblazor": {
              "type": "http",
              "url": "https://izzyblazor.com/mcp"
            }
          }
        }
        """;

    private const string CursorJson = """
        {
          "mcpServers": {
            "izzyblazor": {
              "url": "https://izzyblazor.com/mcp"
            }
          }
        }
        """;
}
